WEBVTT

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:01.370
you tap pay.

00:00:01.370 --> 00:00:02.975
the spinner spins.

00:00:02.975 --> 00:00:04.224
then, nothing.

00:00:04.224 --> 00:00:05.829
did it go through?

00:00:05.829 --> 00:00:08.950
tap again, and you might pay twice.

00:00:09.850 --> 00:00:11.665
robots have the same problem.

00:00:11.665 --> 00:00:14.294
a computer says: move this wheel a little.

00:00:14.294 --> 00:00:15.796
the robot maybe does it.

00:00:15.796 --> 00:00:18.300
and the reply gets lost on the way back.

00:00:19.183 --> 00:00:21.456
send it again, and it might move twice.

00:00:21.456 --> 00:00:23.846
assume it worked, and you might be wrong.

00:00:23.846 --> 00:00:24.837
both are guesses.

00:00:24.837 --> 00:00:28.333
and guessing with machines that move is how things go wrong.

00:00:29.233 --> 00:00:31.104
actryn does something simple.

00:00:31.104 --> 00:00:35.682
every command gets its own id, so it's never mixed up with another one.

00:00:35.682 --> 00:00:38.584
and permission is a timer, not a blank check.

00:00:38.584 --> 00:00:40.583
thirty seconds, then it's gone.

00:00:41.483 --> 00:00:45.021
when the reply goes missing, actryn doesn't guess.

00:00:45.021 --> 00:00:47.993
it writes down the honest answer: unknown.

00:00:47.993 --> 00:00:49.620
and it closes the gate.

00:00:49.620 --> 00:00:52.733
no new commands until a person says recover.

00:00:53.633 --> 00:00:56.733
after recovery, the robot can work again.

00:00:56.733 --> 00:00:59.984
but that lost command stays marked unknown.

00:00:59.984 --> 00:01:00.589
forever.

00:01:00.589 --> 00:01:03.083
nobody gets to pretend it worked.

00:01:03.983 --> 00:01:05.103
that's the idea.

00:01:05.103 --> 00:01:07.483
here's the real software doing it.

00:01:08.083 --> 00:01:12.213
this is actryn version 0.0.1, running in two virtual machines.

00:01:12.213 --> 00:01:15.010
i make the fake controller drop its reply.

00:01:15.010 --> 00:01:16.942
actryn says: outcome unknown.

00:01:16.942 --> 00:01:18.807
the next command is refused.

00:01:18.807 --> 00:01:19.473
i recover.

00:01:19.473 --> 00:01:21.471
the lost one is still unknown.

00:01:21.471 --> 00:01:25.733
the next one completes, and gets checked against the controller.

00:01:27.150 --> 00:01:29.182
nothing physical moved here.

00:01:29.182 --> 00:01:32.229
it's software, and a simulated controller.

00:01:32.229 --> 00:01:34.043
hardware testing is next.

00:01:34.043 --> 00:01:36.800
if you build robots, i'd love to talk.
